>
  <h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
  <p>Tiles are a decoration category used when planning the appearance of restaurant surfaces. This page explains their place in the Wiki and links to broader layout and customization information.</p>

  <h2 id="how-it-works">How It Works</h2>
  <p>Tile choices belong to the visual layer of restaurant planning. Consider them alongside the surrounding furniture, counters, and the separation between dining and kitchen areas.</p>

  <h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>
  <p>Use Tiles to support a consistent visual direction across the restaurant. When working on a larger redesign, plan functional areas first and then review how surface choices fit the finished layout.</p>

  <h2 id="gameplay-tips">Gameplay Tips</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Choose a clear visual direction before changing multiple areas.</li>
    <li>Keep furniture placement and movement paths readable.</li>
    <li>Review the Decorations hub when looking for another customization topic.</li>
    <li>Use the Restaurant Layout Guide for broader space-planning help.</li>
  </ul>
</ContentPage>
